                        <span>PRESS RELEASE</span>
                    
                    
                        <span>October 13, 2026</span>
                    
                    
                </div>

        <div>
                
                
                
                    <h2>
                        
    
        Apple unveils the new Apple&nbsp;TV&nbsp;4K, supercharged by Siri&nbsp;AI
    

                    </h2>
                
            </div>

        <div>
                
                
                    A more capable and conversational Siri, faster performance, and an even more immersive home theater setup elevate the entertainment experience
                
            </div>

        
            
    
    
    
    
    

        

    </div>







    
    
    






  
    
    
    
    
      <figure aria-label="Media, Apple TV 4K is pictured with the Siri Remote.">
        <div>
             
              
              <div>
                The new Apple TV 4K features Siri AI, which transforms how users search for, discover, and enjoy their favorite movies and TV shows; faster performance; and an even more immersive home theater experience.
              </div>
            
            
            
            
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/10/apple-unveils-the-new-apple-tv-4k/article/Apple-TV-4K-261013.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-TV-4K-261013_big" aria-label="Download media, Apple TV 4K is pictured with the Siri Remote."></a>
          </div>
      </figure>
    
  








    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <div><span>CUPERTINO, CALIFORNIA</span> Apple today announced the next generation of <a href="https://www.apple.com/apple-tv-4k/" target="_blank">Apple TV 4K</a>, delivering its most immersive home theater experience yet. The new Apple TV 4K features Siri AI, an entirely new version of Siri powered by the next generation of Apple Intelligence, transforming how users search for, discover, and enjoy their favorite movies and TV shows through a full-screen Siri AI experience.<sup>1</sup> With built-in far-field microphones, Apple TV 4K also lets users talk to Siri completely hands-free.<sup>2</sup>
</div>
                 
             
                 <div>The new Apple TV 4K delivers even faster performance and, when paired with four HomePod mini 2 or HomePod (2nd generation) speakers, unlocks the most immersive home theater surround sound setup Apple has ever offered. As a home hub, Apple TV 4K also makes managing the smart home easier than ever, with Apple Intelligence-generated camera activity descriptions and summarized notifications in the Home app, and control of accessories and scenes.<sup>3</sup>
</div>
                 
             
                 <div>The new Apple TV 4K can be pre-ordered starting today, with availability beginning November 13.
</div>
                 
             
                 <div>“The new Apple TV 4K is our most immersive home theater experience yet,” said Bob Borchers, Apple’s vice president of Worldwide Product Marketing. “With Siri AI, finding something to watch becomes a full-screen, conversational experience, and with built-in far-field microphones, it’s completely hands-free. Pair it with HomePod for the best surround sound setup we’ve ever offered, and it makes managing your Apple Home accessories easier than ever. Now, alongside HomeView, HomePod mini 2, and Apple Home Collection, it’s part of the most connected Apple Home we’ve ever built.”
</div>
                 
             
                 <h2><strong>An Entirely New Version of Siri Powered by Apple&nbsp;Intelligence</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>Apple TV 4K brings Siri AI to the living room with a rich, full-screen experience. An entirely new version of Siri powered by the next generation of Apple Intelligence, Siri AI is a profoundly more capable and conversational assistant with personal context understanding, broad world knowledge, and the ability to take even more systemwide app actions, making it effortless to find entertainment. Users can simply ask Siri “What Apple TV shows won at the Emmy Awards this year?” and see beautiful poster art pulled directly from the Apple TV app, along with relevant suggestions like “More award-winning comedies” to keep exploring. While watching, users can ask Siri AI follow-up questions and tap into Siri AI’s broad world knowledge to go deeper into a show, asking things like “Where was <em>Pluribus</em> filmed?” or “Is this appropriate for a 15-year-old?” Responses appear in a compact, subtle overlay, providing helpful information when viewers ask while keeping them immersed in the action. With an Apple Intelligence-enabled iPhone, Siri AI on Apple TV 4K can now tap into a user’s personal context to answer requests like “Play the show Alinda recommended.”
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    






  
    
    
    
    
      <figure aria-label="Media, Apple TV 4K displays a Siri AI message with thumbnails to various documentaries. The message reads, “Here are some nature documentaries available on Apple TV, including ‘Prehistoric Planet,’ ‘The Elephant Queen,’ and ‘Earthsounds.’”">
        <div>
             
              
              <div>
                Siri AI is a profoundly more capable and conversational assistant with personal context understanding, broad world knowledge, and the ability to take even more systemwide app actions, making it effortless to find entertainment.
              </div>
            
            
            
            
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/10/apple-unveils-the-new-apple-tv-4k/article/Apple-TV-4K-with-Siri-AI-suggestions-261013.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-TV-4K-with-Siri-AI-suggestions-261013_big" aria-label="Download media, Apple TV 4K displays a Siri AI message with thumbnails to various documentaries. The message reads, “Here are some nature documentaries available on Apple TV, including ‘Prehistoric Planet,’ ‘The Elephant Queen,’ and ‘Earthsounds.’”"></a>
          </div>
      </figure>
    
  








    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>A Fully Hands-Free Experience with Far-Field Microphones</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>The new Apple TV 4K features three far-field microphones, letting users control what they’re watching and discover new shows completely hands-free. Advanced echo cancellation intelligently isolates a user’s voice from background sound to deliver crystal-clear “Hey Siri” or “Siri” recognition, even while audio is playing.
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    


    
    <div data-component-list="ScrollAnimationDefault AutoPlayVideo">
        <div>Apple TV 4K now features three far-field microphones, letting users control what they’re watching and discover new shows completely hands-free.</div>
        
            <a aria-label="Download video: Far-Field Microphones on Apple TV 4K" data-analytics-title="Download video - Far-Field Microphones on Apple TV 4K" download="" href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/videos/2026/autoplay/10/apple-tv-4k-far-field-microphones/downloads/Apple-TV-4K-far-field-microphones-261013.zip">
            </a>
        
    </div>






    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>Faster Performance, Smarter Remote</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>The A19 chip in the new Apple TV 4K delivers up to 50 percent faster CPU performance and up to 2x faster GPU performance than the previous generation, for greater responsiveness, faster navigation, and smoother animations. The A19 chip also includes a new, dedicated AV1 decoder, enabling more efficient, high-quality streaming while using less bandwidth.
</div>
                 
             
                 <div>The new Siri Remote keeps its familiar design while adding Find My support with Precision Finding and an option to play a sound on the remote — making it far easier to locate.<sup>4</sup>
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    


    
        
        
        
        
            <figure aria-label="Media, An iPhone 18 Pro screen shows Find My locating a Siri Remote, with the message “80 ft ahead.”">
                <div>
                         
                            
                            <div>
                                The Siri Remote adds Find My support with Precision Finding and an option to play a sound, making it far easier to locate.
                            </div>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/10/apple-unveils-the-new-apple-tv-4k/article/Apple-TV-4K-Siri-Remote-Precision-Finding-261013.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-TV-4K-Siri-Remote-Precision-Finding-261013_inline" aria-label="Download media, An iPhone 18 Pro screen shows Find My locating a Siri Remote, with the message “80 ft ahead.”"></a>
                    </div>
            </figure>
        
    












    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>Apple’s Most Immersive Home Theater Ever</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>Pairing HomePod with Apple TV 4K already offers users an immersive viewing experience that’s easy to set up, and the new Apple TV 4K takes it even further. For the first time, users can create a four-speaker surround sound experience with Apple TV 4K (4th generation) and HomePod mini 2. The four speakers work together with Apple TV 4K to intelligently recognize their position in the room so audio timing and levels are automatically calibrated to the space. HomePod (2nd generation) can also be used in this four-speaker setup for the ultimate audio experience, as long as the front and rear speaker pairs match.<sup>5</sup>
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    






  
    
    
    
    
      <figure aria-label="Media, Apple TV 4K and a four-speaker setup, with two HomePod (2nd generation) speakers in the front and two HomePod mini 2 speakers in the rear.">
        <div>
             
              
              <div>
                For the first time, users can create a four-speaker surround sound experience with HomePod.
              </div>
            
            
            
            
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/10/apple-unveils-the-new-apple-tv-4k/article/Apple-TV-4K-home-theater-setup-261013.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-TV-4K-home-theater-setup-261013_big" aria-label="Download media, Apple TV 4K and a four-speaker setup, with two HomePod (2nd generation) speakers in the front and two HomePod mini 2 speakers in the rear."></a>
          </div>
      </figure>
    
  








    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>An Even Smarter Home Hub</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>The new Apple TV 4K continues to serve as a powerful home hub, giving users control of their smart home accessories from anywhere.<sup>6</sup> With a compatible doorbell, notifications appear directly on the TV so users can see who’s at the door, speak with them, and control other accessories like unlocking the door — all without interrupting what they’re watching. Apple TV 4K supports automations, guest mode, and secure local processing of HomeKit Secure Video, now enhanced with Apple Intelligence-generated camera activity video descriptions and summarized notifications. Users can also use Siri AI to control smart home accessories and turn scenes on or off hands-free. And with built-in Wi-Fi and Thread, Apple TV 4K can seamlessly connect and control a user’s smart home.
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    


    
        
        
        
        
            <figure aria-label="Media, Apple TV 4K displays a user’s smart home controls.">
                <div>
                         
                            
                            <div>
                                Apple TV 4K is a powerful home hub, giving users control of their smart home accessories from anywhere.
                            </div>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/10/apple-unveils-the-new-apple-tv-4k/article/Apple-TV-4K-home-hub-261013.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-TV-4K-home-hub-261013_inline" aria-label="Download media, Apple TV 4K displays a user’s smart home controls."></a>
                    </div>
            </figure>
        
    












    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>More Ways to Enjoy the Living Room</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>Apple TV 4K is more than just a way to watch — it’s a home essential that transforms the living room to reflect what users want in the moment. With Apple Fitness+, the living room becomes a workout studio, while Apple Arcade and the App Store’s library of games turn it into a home arcade. With the Apple TV app, users can stream hundreds of Apple Originals, including thrilling dramas, epic sci-fi, and feel-good comedies, as well as live sports such as Formula 1® in the U.S., Major League Soccer, and Friday Night Baseball.<sup>7</sup> Users can also make FaceTime calls with Continuity Camera, view photos, and do even more, all from the big screen.<sup>8</sup> With an iPhone or iPad, users can now customize how their iCloud photos appear on Apple TV, making it easy to set up personalized Memories &amp; Slideshows or Portraits screen savers without making their entire library visible. Plus, a new screen saver shuffle feature automatically rotates between categories so there is always something new to see.
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    


    
    
        
        
        
