        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>Private and Secure by Design</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>Like every Apple product, Apple TV 4K is designed with privacy and security in mind. Apple TV 4K and the A19 chip include Secure Exclaves: protected and compartmentalized runtimes used to process microphone data separately from the rest of the system. Isolation features added across many core components of the silicon work in tandem to protect Secure Exclaves and keep them segregated from the rest of the system. Data that is processed and analyzed in the Secure Exclaves cannot be accessed by tvOS, apps, the user, or Apple.
</div>
                 
             
                 <div>Siri AI takes full advantage of the bold new architecture for Apple Intelligence. Siri requests on Apple TV 4K can use on-device processing or Private Cloud Compute, which extends the privacy of the device to the cloud. When processed in Private Cloud Compute, data is neither stored nor made accessible to Apple or anyone else. HomeKit Secure Video footage is stored end-to-end encrypted and never accessible to Apple.
</div>
                 
             
                 <h2><strong>Apple TV 4K and the Environment</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>Apple TV 4K was built with the environment in mind and drives progress toward Apple’s ambitious plan to be carbon neutral across its entire footprint by 2030. Apple TV 4K features 100 percent recycled gold plating and tin solder in all Apple-designed printed circuit boards, and 100 percent recycled rare earth elements in all magnets. The thermal module is made with 80 percent recycled aluminum, while the enclosure of the Siri Remote includes 100 percent recycled aluminum. Apple TV 4K meets Apple’s high standards for energy efficiency and safe chemistry. As with all Apple products, its paper packaging is 100 percent fiber-based<sup>9</sup> and designed to be recycled.
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 
                 
             
                 <div><ul>
<li>Customers in the U.S. and 29 other countries and regions can pre-order Apple TV 4K (4th generation) starting today from <a href="https://www.apple.com/store" target="_blank">apple.com/store</a> and in the Apple Store app, with availability in stores beginning Friday, November 13.</li>
</ul>
</div>
                 
             
                 <div><ul>
<li>Apple TV 4K (4th generation) is available for <strong>$299 </strong>(U.S.) or <strong>$49.83</strong> (U.S.) per month for six months.<sup>10</sup></li>
</ul>
</div>
                 
             
                 <div><ul>
<li>Siri AI is available as a beta on Apple TV 4K (2nd generation or later), and is available at launch in the <em>U.S.</em>,<em> Australia</em>, <em>Canada</em>, <em>India</em>, <em>New Zealand</em>, <em>Singapore</em>, <em>South Africa</em>, and the <em>UK </em>in English.</li>
</ul>
</div>
                 
             
                 <div><ul>
<li>The new Siri Remote is compatible with Apple TV HD and Apple TV 4K, and is also available for purchase separately. Find My support is available on the Siri Remote (2nd generation or later).</li>
</ul>
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    




    
    
        
    


    
    
    



    
    
    




    




    
    
    





    
    
    <div>
            <ol>
<li>Some features may not be available in all regions or languages. Some devices may not be available in all regions. Siri AI is available in beta in tvOS 27.2 and requires the owner of the home in the Home app to have an Apple Intelligence-enabled iPhone or iPad running the latest software version and have Siri AI turned on and set to a supported language. Personal context requests require a paired Apple Intelligence-enabled device with Siri AI turned on and set to a supported language. Siri AI will not be initially available in the EU in iOS or iPadOS. Certain Apple Intelligence features that rely on server-side models are subject to daily usage limits. Expanded access to such features will be available for a fee in the future. Use of these features is subject to the Apple Intelligence terms and conditions. Learn more at <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/148587" target="_blank">support.apple.com/148587</a>. Access to Siri AI is also available on Apple TV 4K (2nd generation) or later.</li>
<li>Far-field microphone support for Siri varies by region and language. Supported when the primary tvOS language is set to Mandarin Chinese, Dutch, English, Finnish, French, German, Hebrew, Norwegian, or Swedish.</li>
<li>Video descriptions for HomeKit Secure Video camera recordings require setup using an Apple Intelligence-enabled iPhone or iPad and a subscription to an eligible iCloud+ plan. Some Apple Intelligence features in the Home app, such as video summaries, are available for a limited number of cameras depending on the iCloud+ plan. Supported camera counts and other iCloud+ plan features may change over time. Learn more at <a href="https://www.apple.com/apple-intelligence/" target="_blank">apple.com/apple-intelligence</a>.</li>
<li>Find My support is available on the Siri Remote (2nd generation or later). Precision Finding works on the Siri Remote (4th generation) paired with iPhone Duo, iPhone Air, or iPhone 17 or later (excluding iPhone 17e) running the latest iOS software; availability varies by region. Playing a sound to locate the remote is exclusive to the newest Siri Remote.</li>
<li>Home theater surround sound requires four HomePod (2nd generation) or HomePod mini 2 speakers in matching pairs (front and rear), paired with Apple TV 4K (4th generation) running the latest operating system software.</li>
<li>Compatible smart home accessories sold separately.</li>
<li>Subscription may be required to access some content. Live sports subject to blackouts. Title and application availability subject to change. Some applications are not available in all areas.</li>
<li>Available on compatible iPhone and iPad devices with Apple TV 4K (2nd generation or later) running the latest operating system software.</li>
<li>Breakdown of U.S. retail packaging by weight. Adhesives, inks, and coatings are excluded from Apple’s calculations.</li>
<li>Apple Card Monthly Installments (ACMI) is a 0 percent APR payment option that is only available if users select it at checkout in the U.S. for eligible products purchased at Apple and is subject to credit approval and credit limit. See <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102730" target="_blank">support.apple.com/en-us/102730</a> for more information about eligible products. Additional limits and restrictions apply. See the Apple Card Customer Agreement for more information about ACMI. Apple Card is subject to credit approval, available only for qualifying applicants in the United States, and issued by Goldman Sachs Bank USA, Salt Lake City Branch.</li>
</ol>

        </div>



    
    
    






    















	

		
		
			
























		
		

