            <title><![CDATA[11 year old unsoundness bugs found in Rust borrow checker (489 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/164250</link>
            <guid>50069499</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:27:00 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/164250">https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/164250</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50069499">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div><div data-testid="issue-viewer-issue-container" data-hpc="true" containertiming="hpc" tabindex="-1"><h2>Description</h2><div><div><p><a data-component="Link" href="https://github.com/jsnell" aria-label="@jsnell's profile"><img data-component="Avatar" alt="@jsnell" width="24" height="24" src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/608702?v=4&amp;size=48" data-testid="github-avatar"></a></p></div><div data-testid="issue-body-viewer" data-team-hovercards-enabled="true" data-turbolinks="false" id="issue-body-viewer"><p dir="auto">In the following code:</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="use std::sync::Mutex;
static KEPT: Mutex<Vec<Box<dyn std::any::Any + Send>>> = Mutex::new(Vec::new());
struct Q<T: 'static + Send>(Option<T>);
impl<T: 'static + Send> Drop for Q<T> {
    fn drop(&amp;mut self) { if let Some(t) = self.0.take() { KEPT.lock().unwrap().push(Box::new(t)); } }
}
fn main() {
    {
        let l = String::from(&quot;hello world, this is long enough&quot;);
        let mut q = Q(None);
        q.0 = Some(&amp;l);
    }
    let _z = String::from(&quot;XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX&quot;);
    let k = KEPT.lock().unwrap();
    println!(&quot;{}&quot;, k[0].downcast_ref::<&amp;'static String>().unwrap());
}"><pre><span>use</span> std<span>::</span>sync<span>::</span><span>Mutex</span><span>;</span>
<span>static</span> <span>KEPT</span><span>:</span> <span>Mutex</span><span>&lt;</span><span>Vec</span><span>&lt;</span><span>Box</span><span>&lt;</span><span>dyn</span> std<span>::</span>any<span>::</span><span>Any</span> + <span>Send</span><span>&gt;</span><span>&gt;</span><span>&gt;</span> = <span>Mutex</span><span>::</span><span>new</span><span>(</span><span>Vec</span><span>::</span><span>new</span><span>(</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>
<span>struct</span> <span>Q</span><span>&lt;</span><span>T</span><span>:</span> <span>'</span><span>static</span> + <span>Send</span><span>&gt;</span><span>(</span><span>Option</span><span>&lt;</span><span>T</span><span>&gt;</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>
<span>impl</span><span>&lt;</span><span>T</span><span>:</span> <span>'</span><span>static</span> + <span>Send</span><span>&gt;</span> <span>Drop</span> <span>for</span> <span>Q</span><span>&lt;</span><span>T</span><span>&gt;</span> <span>{</span>
    <span>fn</span> <span>drop</span><span>(</span><span>&amp;</span><span>mut</span> <span>self</span><span>)</span> <span>{</span> <span>if</span> <span>let</span> <span>Some</span><span>(</span>t<span>)</span> = <span>self</span><span>.</span><span>0</span><span>.</span><span>take</span><span>(</span><span>)</span> <span>{</span> <span>KEPT</span><span>.</span><span>lock</span><span>(</span><span>)</span><span>.</span><span>unwrap</span><span>(</span><span>)</span><span>.</span><span>push</span><span>(</span><span>Box</span><span>::</span><span>new</span><span>(</span>t<span>)</span><span>)</span><span>;</span> <span>}</span> <span>}</span>
<span>}</span>
<span>fn</span> <span>main</span><span>(</span><span>)</span> <span>{</span>
    <span>{</span>
        <span>let</span> l = <span>String</span><span>::</span><span>from</span><span>(</span><span>"hello world, this is long enough"</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>
        <span>let</span> <span>mut</span> q = <span>Q</span><span>(</span><span>None</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>
        q<span>.</span><span>0</span> = <span>Some</span><span>(</span><span>&amp;</span>l<span>)</span><span>;</span>
    <span>}</span>
    <span>let</span> _z = <span>String</span><span>::</span><span>from</span><span>(</span><span>"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>
    <span>let</span> k = <span>KEPT</span><span>.</span><span>lock</span><span>(</span><span>)</span><span>.</span><span>unwrap</span><span>(</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>
    <span>println</span><span>!</span><span>(</span><span>"{}"</span><span>,</span> k<span>[</span><span>0</span><span>]</span><span>.</span>downcast_ref<span>::</span>&lt;<span>&amp;</span><span>'</span><span>static</span> <span>String</span>&gt;<span>(</span><span>)</span><span>.</span>unwrap<span>(</span><span>)</span><span>)</span><span>;</span>
<span>}</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">I expected to see this happen: program is not accepted</p>
<p dir="auto">Instead, this happened: program compiles and prints <code>XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX</code>. With asan, the program will crash with a <code>AddressSanitizer: stack-use-after-scope</code></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Meta</h3>
<p dir="auto">Issue on current nightly, and stables at least down to 1.85.0</p>
<p dir="auto">Godbolt with asan: <a href="https://rust.godbolt.org/z/83MvfbKde" rel="nofollow">https://rust.godbolt.org/z/83MvfbKde</a><br>
Godbolt without asan: <a href="https://rust.godbolt.org/z/GsGdqqMWe" rel="nofollow">https://rust.godbolt.org/z/GsGdqqMWe</a></p></div></div></div><!--$--><div data-testid="issue-viewer-comments-container"><h2 id="_R_31st685_">Activity</h2><ol id="issue-timeline" data-testid="issue-timeline-container" aria-labelledby="_R_31st685_" role="list"><li data-timeline-event-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHteHOOA" data-highlighted-event="false" data-testid="timeline-row-border-LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHteHOOA" data-wrapper-timeline-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHteHOOA"></li><li data-timeline-event-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHteHUIg" data-highlighted-event="false" data-testid="timeline-row-border-LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHteHUIg" data-wrapper-timeline-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHteHUIg"></li><li data-timeline-event-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHtfZEow" data-highlighted-event="false" data-testid="timeline-row-border-LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHtfZEow" data-wrapper-timeline-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHtfZEow"></li><li data-timeline-event-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHtfZN_A" data-highlighted-event="false" data-testid="timeline-row-border-LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHtfZN_A" data-wrapper-timeline-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHtfZN_A"></li><li data-timeline-event-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHtfgFoQ" data-highlighted-event="false" data-testid="timeline-row-border-LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHtfgFoQ" data-wrapper-timeline-id="LE_lADOAAsO6M8AAAABW1X2hM8AAAAHtfgFoQ"></li><li data-wrapper-timeline-id="IC_kwDOAAsO6M8AAAABbhqk7A"><div data-testid="timeline-row-border-IC_kwDOAAsO6M8AAAABbhqk7A" data-timeline-event-id="IC_kwDOAAsO6M8AAAABbhqk7A" data-highlighted-event="false"><div id="issuecomment-6142207212" data-testid="comment-header"><h3>theemathas<!-- --> <!-- -->commented<!-- --> <relative-time data-component="RelativeTime">on<!-- --> <!-- -->Oct 13, 2026<!-- --> </relative-time></h3><p><a data-component="Link" href="https://github.com/theemathas" aria-label="@theemathas's profile"><img data-component="Avatar" alt="@theemathas" width="24" height="24" src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6120103?v=4&amp;size=48" data-testid="github-avatar"></a></p></div><div><div data-testid="markdown-body" data-team-hovercards-enabled="true" data-turbolinks="false"><p dir="auto">The core of the unsoundness:</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="struct Q<T: 'static>(Option<T>);

impl<T: 'static> Drop for Q<T> {
    fn drop(&amp;mut self) {
        // Code in here has access to a non-'static &amp;String
