<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div data-hpc="true" containertiming="hpc"><article itemprop="text">
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://github.com/prabanta-dev/janas/blob/main"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/25a3d40ed8ebb245dd21217765a2df66b3e7ad3f172d1f5266482bbad2ab2054/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f7374617475732d6578706572696d656e74616c2d6f72616e67652e737667" alt="Status: experimental" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/badge/status-experimental-orange.svg"></a> <a href="https://github.com/prabanta-dev/janas/blob/main"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/424b3417ce597434dd6aca4df86b67ef28653e5d9f5fef430c243f5a1b1e3131/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f706c6174666f726d2d4c696e757825323025374325323057696e646f77732532307838362d2d36342d6c69676874677265792e737667" alt="Platform: Linux | Windows x86-64" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/badge/platform-Linux%20%7C%20Windows%20x86--64-lightgrey.svg"></a> <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maurizio-cammalleri-80a89a11/" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/86e545539b80dee37f66ed7c72f1589aed5545cd0207aede6ea4f3ad5e31e53b/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f4c696e6b6564496e2d4d617572697a696f25323043616d6d616c6c6572692d3030373742353f6c6f676f3d6c696e6b6564696e" alt="LinkedIn" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/badge/LinkedIn-Maurizio%20Cammalleri-0077B5?logo=linkedin"></a> <a href="https://cammalleri.substack.com/" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/29cdd19e7d27cb7c3f08edcb1392b2ecee8dedbdd28ca798377c4f18e9756479/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f537562737461636b2d4d617572697a696f25323043616d6d616c6c6572692d4646363731393f6c6f676f3d737562737461636b" alt="Substack" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Substack-Maurizio%20Cammalleri-FF6719?logo=substack"></a></p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>37 tok/s from Qwen3-Next-80B (a 48 GB model) on a laptop with 32 GB of memory, 24 without drafts, where llama.cpp manages 2.8; reading a prompt, 62 tok/s against 16.</strong> Janas-LLM was faster than llama.cpp on every model compared on the same laptop (Debian 13 Linux, Intel Core Ultra 9 185H, its integrated Arc GPU, 32 GB, an NVMe SSD; 9-11 October 2026; the whole machine <a href="#the-machine-it-grew-on">below</a>):</p>
