<p dir="auto"><code>janas-server</code> fills in code at an editor's cursor, with a model for code such as Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B: OpenAI's <code>/v1/completions</code> with a <code>suffix</code>, and llama.cpp's <code>/infill</code>, which llama.vscode asks. The window sent at every keystroke is kept from moving, so that a keystroke reads only what it changed: 1.5-2.2 s a proposal on a laptop, where a window slid a line was read again in 17 s. How to set it up in VSCodium and VS Code, with llama.vscode or Continue, and what was measured: <a href="https://github.com/prabanta-dev/janas/blob/main/docs/code-completion.md">docs/code-completion.md</a>.</p>
